new file mode 100644
index 00000000..0659f9cf
--- /dev/null
+++ b/contracts/recipes/tapestry-recipe.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,563 @@
+# tapestry-recipe.yaml is loom's producer graph. It is embedded into the binary by the sibling
+# recipes.go rather than read from disk. The row names below are the durable on-disk
+# identities pinned against internal/loomshed's Name* constants by the coverage guard -- a rename
+# here without a matching constant rename breaks resume for any in-flight task.
+#
+# The main line is Preflight, Tapestry-Preflight, Discussion-Write, the Discussion-Review ring,
+# Drift-Baseline, Plan-Write, the Plan-Review ring, Drift-Await, Webster, Parent-Align, the
+# Code-Review ring, Drift-Verify, Describe, PR-Review, Finalize and Friction-Reflect.
+# The three Drift rows carry entry_gate: drift.enabled, so a hub that leaves regression off records
+# each of them Skipped and spawns or runs nothing for them.
+#
+# Every gate and validator bounces back to the producer whose artifact it guards, and a gate whose
+# guarded artifact is produced by no row in the list escalates instead.
+# Preflight and Tapestry-Preflight carry no on_stuck for exactly that reason: nothing in the list
+# produces what each of them gates, so a human is the only thing that can fix either.
+# Parent-Align and Finalize carry none either, because each fixes its own merge and test failures in its
+# merge fixer, and a failure the fixer cannot fix halts the run for the orch instead of routing to another row.
+#
+# Those four are not the whole escalate-to-a-human set, and the difference matters when auditing
+# routing from this header.
+# These PRODUCER rows also carry no on_stuck -- Discussion-Write, Drift-Baseline, Plan-Write,
+# Drift-Await, Webster, Drift-Verify, Describe and PR-Review -- and their Stuck halts the whole run just
+# as a gate's does.
+# PR-Review carries no entry_gate either: whether it opens a pull request reads the parent's anchor, a
+# board field and the origin, which the row decides in its own call.
+# A gated writer row's exhausted gate halts the run for a human rather than bouncing to a fresh
+# writer, deliberately: after three in-session re-prompts with the findings already in hand,
+# a cold respawn that knows nothing about the complaint is strictly worse than stopping and telling
+# someone.
+#
+# Webster's Stuck halts the run for a human too, with one exception: Webster declares on_reroute:
+# Plan-Burler-Review, and its producer marks a Stuck Reroute only when begin-batch left a new
+# plan-conflict record.
+# Finalize declares on_reroute: Parent-Align, the edge a spent fixer change, or an over-cap one its
+# fix review does not approve, takes when a review follows.
+# Shed's reroute cap bounds that edge, and a reroute spends no bounce budget.
+#
+# Friction-Reflect is outside the escalate-to-a-human set: it also carries no on_stuck, but it always
+# returns Done and never Stuck.
+#
+# Parent-Align follows Webster and brings the parent's upstream tip into the task branch with no parent
+# lock, then hands to the Code-Review perch.
+# Finalize takes the parent lock first and is the only row that lands on the parent.
+#
+# Drift-Verify compares the code after the Code-Review perch with the baseline Drift-Baseline captured
+# on the branch point, and spawns one agent to judge, accept and fix drift. Its fixes are not
+# reviewed again. A Finalize reroute re-enters it through Parent-Align and the Code-Review perch,
+# and the Code-Review perch's own fixes reach it as the code it compares.
+# Drift-Await holds Webster until the baseline capture passed or the parent deferred it.
+#
+# An in-flight run parked on a row this recipe removed or renamed -- Webster-Bouncer and its
+# Burler rows, Merge-Bouncer and its Burler rows, Publish, PR-Align, PR-Gate or PR-Rework -- or on a
+# row whose edges changed with them, is restarted, not migrated: row names are durable on-disk
+# resume identities, and a permanent migration table mapping retired names onto their successors is
+# carrying cost a pre-release, single-operator system does not need when the operator can simply
+# re-run.
+# A run parked on Merge-In, the row now named Parent-Align, or on Loom-Preflight, the row now named
+# Tapestry-Preflight, is carried across by rename and not restarted: `lym loom` rewrites the old name
+# in its status file through TapestryRetiredRows, and the row keeps its position, so `lym loom peers`
+# reports the same positions.
+#
+# Every review segment follows the same shared-segment on_stuck ring: Discussion-Bouncer,
+# Discussion-Burler-Review and Discussion-Burler-Fix carry segment: Discussion-Review, the three
+# Plan rows carry segment: Plan-Review, and the three Code rows carry segment: Code-Review.
+# A review segment's rows also share one role_prefix, which leads their sessions' roles,
+# so ly:<slug>:plan-burler-review names its segment.
+# In each ring the Bouncer's on_stuck names the review row, the review row's on_stuck names the fix
+# row, and the fix row's on_stuck names the Bouncer, and each Burler row's on_done names the same
+# row as its on_stuck -- neither Burler row ever returns Done, and an empty on_done would end the
+# run silently. A Done by any row of a segment ends its bounce episode, so the hand-offs between
+# the two halves are Stucks. internal/shedengine's validator rejects an OnStuck naming a producer
+# in a different Segment, so each ring needs its own non-empty, shared label for its edges to build
+# at all.
+#
+# A review segment's round is two Shed rows, each one fresh session: the review row reviews, and
+# the fix row fixes only a review with findings, or a clean review whose row gates fail. The
+# reviewer's findings carry their own fix, so the fixer orients on the review and its targets alone.
+#
+# An in-flight run parked on one of the retired Discussion-Burler or Plan-Burler rows is restarted,
+# not migrated, as it is for the retired rows above.
+#
+# So is a run parked on the retired Batchifier row: the Webster row's implementer partitions the
+# plan itself, and Tapestry-Preflight's batcher.yaml load keeps the early failure the row gave.
+#
+# The Bouncer, review and fix rows of those segments declare no max_bounces: their budget is the
+# perch's own loom.yaml key (discussion_max_bounces, plan_max_bounces or code_max_bounces),
+# an absent per-perch budget takes review_max_bounces, and a perch at 0 keeps its route while its
+# Bouncer settles at once, applied by internal/loomrecipe.
+
+version: 1
+entry: Preflight
+# The arbiter's prompt names this row once the plan is approved: a decision that amends the plan routes here.
+amendment_target: Plan-Burler-Review
+terminals:
+  - Friction-Reflect
+
+producers:
+  - name: Preflight
+    engine: Preflight
+    on_done: Tapestry-Preflight
+
+  - name: Tapestry-Preflight
+    engine: TapestryPreflight
+    on_done: Discussion-Write
+
+  - name: Discussion-Write
+    engine: DiscussionWrite
+    on_done: Discussion-Bouncer
+    config:
+      # gates holds this row's handoff until the artifact is mechanically valid: each entry names a
+      # validator and re-prompts the live session up to its attempts times, so a failure never
+      # reaches the row below.
+      gates:
+        - name: discussion
+          attempts: 3
+
+  - name: Discussion-Bouncer
+    engine: Bouncer
+    segment: Discussion-Review
+    on_stuck: Discussion-Burler-Review
+    on_done: Drift-Baseline
+    config:
+      run_subdir: discussion
+      subject: document
+      role_prefix: discussion
+      reviewer_fan_setting: loom.discussion_reviewer_fan
+      auto_accept_setting: loom.discussion_auto_accept
+      artifact_paths:
+        - _lym/discussion/decision-record.md
+        - _lym/discussion/support-log.md
+      rubric_stencil: loom-rubric-discussion-review
+      # commit_seam is required rather than optional here: Discussion-Burler-Fix runs fix-scope: overlay
+      # and an overlay round runs no git at all, and nothing else in this segment commits, so without
+      # the seam every approved fix would stay uncommitted in fabric's records working tree.
+      commit_seam: discussion
+      # carry_over names this row's own segment: the Bouncer files the round's still-open findings
+      # under it in the decision record's Open risks section, and a test pins it equal to segment.
+      carry_over: Discussion-Review
+      # escalate_decisions makes this Bouncer send a round's decision-class findings to the run's
+      # parent; Discussion-Burler-Fix sets decisions_escalated so its fixer is given none and
+      # posts no notice of its own, and a test pins the two set together.
+      escalate_decisions: true
+      # No model/effort/version key: the row refuses them as unknown keys, and loom.yaml's judge,
+      # seed and per-segment judge and seed keys are the only source of this row's passes' models.
+
+  - name: Discussion-Burler-Review
+    engine: BurlerReview
+    segment: Discussion-Review
+    on_stuck: Discussion-Burler-Fix
+    # BurlerReviewProducer never returns Done, so this edge is unreachable -- but an empty on_done
+    # is load-bearing and ends the whole run silently, which is a worse failure than a redundant
+    # edge, so it is set explicitly to the row it can never actually reach.
+    on_done: Discussion-Burler-Fix
+    config:
+      # The same run_subdir value as Discussion-Bouncer is what makes the three rows write into one
+      # shared run directory.
+      run_subdir: discussion
+      role_prefix: discussion
+      reviewer_fan_setting: loom.discussion_reviewer_fan
+      fixer_fan_setting: loom.discussion_fixer_fan
+      profile:
+        target:
+          paths:
+            - _lym/discussion/decision-record.md
+            - _lym/discussion/support-log.md
+        fasit:
+          instructions: >
+            The authority for this round is the rubric supplied in the prompt. The mechanical
+            section contract over the discussion artifact pair is already enforced by this round's
+            own gate over this round's own output, so re-deriving it here is duplicated work.
+        rubric_stencil: loom-rubric-discussion-review
+        # fix-scope: overlay, not source: the target paths above are fabric records content reached through the
+        # junction, and the Fabric Git Invariant reserves committing that class of file to the loop
+        # owner, never an agent. Discussion-Bouncer's commit_seam: discussion key is what actually
+        # commits this round's approved settle.
+        fix-scope: overlay
+        tool-use: true
+      # No model/effort key: model choice lives in loom.yaml's reviewer and fixer model keys only.
+      # No timeout_s key, for the same Env fallback reason as Discussion-Bouncer.
+
+  - name: Discussion-Burler-Fix
+    engine: BurlerFix
+    segment: Discussion-Review
+    on_stuck: Discussion-Bouncer
+    # BurlerFixProducer never returns Done, so this edge is unreachable -- but an empty on_done is
+    # load-bearing and ends the whole run silently, which is a worse failure than a redundant edge,
+    # so it is set explicitly to the row it can never actually reach.
+    on_done: Discussion-Bouncer
+    config:
+      run_subdir: discussion
+      role_prefix: discussion
+      fixer_fan_setting: loom.discussion_fixer_fan
+      # decisions_escalated says Discussion-Bouncer's escalate_decisions sends the round's
+      # decision-class findings to the parent, so this row keeps them out of the fixer's work
+      # and posts no notice of its own.
+      decisions_escalated: true
+      # review_row names this segment's review row, which a refusal's way forward sends the
+      # operator back to.
+      review_row: Discussion-Burler-Review
+      # gates holds this row's handoff until the artifact is mechanically valid: each entry names a
+      # validator and re-prompts the live session up to its attempts times, so a failure never
+      # reaches the row below.
+      gates:
+        - name: discussion
+          attempts: 3
+      profile:
+        target:
+          paths:
+            - _lym/discussion/decision-record.md
+            - _lym/discussion/support-log.md
+        # fix-scope: overlay, for the reason the review row gives.
+        fix-scope: overlay
+
+  # Drift-Baseline has an agent record the task's regression scope and takes the baseline capture
+  # while the plan is written. Its Stuck halts the run, with the ways forward in its reason.
+  - name: Drift-Baseline
+    engine: DriftBaseline
+    entry_gate: drift.enabled
+    on_done: Plan-Write
+    config:
+      subject: decision-record
+
+  - name: Plan-Write
+    engine: PlanWrite
+    on_done: Plan-Bouncer
+    config:
+      # gates holds this row's handoff until the artifact is mechanically valid: each entry names a
+      # validator and re-prompts the live session up to its attempts times, so a failure never
+      # reaches the row below.
+      gates:
+        - name: plan
+          attempts: 3
+
+  - name: Plan-Bouncer
+    engine: Bouncer
+    segment: Plan-Review
+    on_stuck: Plan-Burler-Review
+    on_done: Drift-Await
+    config:
+      run_subdir: plan
+      subject: document
+      role_prefix: plan
+      reviewer_fan_setting: loom.plan_reviewer_fan
+      auto_accept_setting: loom.plan_auto_accept
+      # A plan is 00-overview.md plus a variable number of card files, so no enumeration written
+      # here stays correct across plans -- the single directory entry is what stays right. Both
+      # consumers accept a directory: shedadapters.NewBouncer stats nothing, and burlerengine's own
+      # path check documents that a file and a directory both satisfy it.
+      artifact_paths:
+        - _lym/plan
+      rubric_stencil: loom-rubric-plan-review
+      # commit_seam is required rather than optional here: Plan-Burler-Fix runs fix-scope: overlay and
+      # an overlay round runs no git at all, and nothing else in this segment commits, so without
+      # the seam every approved fix would stay uncommitted in fabric's records working tree.
+      commit_seam: plan
+      # approve_seam: plan is set on this row and no other -- it is the only row in the whole list
+      # that knows the plan passed review. The approved settle writes the approval flag through
+      # this seam immediately before commit_seam fires, so the flag lands inside the commit rather
+      # than as working-tree dirt afterwards. Neither Discussion-Bouncer nor Code-Bouncer gets
+      # this key: neither of their artifacts carries an approval flag, and an absent key leaves the
+      # seam nil exactly as an omitted commit_seam already does.
+      approve_seam: plan
+      # skip_seam: rework-exempt lets a rework generation whose cards are all exempt pass without a
+      # judge. Its inputs are agent-written -- the overview's first_card and a swept record.json --
+      # so the seam re-classifies the live committed cards: a stale or forged record can at most
+      # skip a generation whose live cards are themselves exempt. It also re-classifies the
+      # working-tree cards, since a Plan-Burler-Fix fix lands only through the commit a skip runs.
+      # Generation 0 never skips, and a seam error falls back to a real review.
+      skip_seam: rework-exempt
+      # carry_over names this row's own segment: the Bouncer files the round's still-open findings
+      # under it in the decision record's Open risks section, and a test pins it equal to segment.
+      carry_over: Plan-Review
+      # No model/effort/version key: the row refuses them as unknown keys, and loom.yaml's judge,
+      # seed and per-segment judge and seed keys are the only source of this row's passes' models.
+
+  - name: Plan-Burler-Review
+    engine: BurlerReview
+    segment: Plan-Review
+    on_stuck: Plan-Burler-Fix
+    # BurlerReviewProducer never returns Done, so this edge is unreachable -- but an empty on_done
